    "summary": "I built the charging station as one closed hex box with a cable-pass-through lid, and it passed every check with no collisions. It's a full hex base (about 191 × 169 mm across, 80 mm tall) with solid end caps on all six sides and a cable-type cover on top. The joints are bolted. A charger and spare cable can sit inside, and the cable comes up through the lid to a phone resting on top. The phone shown on the lid is only there for display. It's 11 printed parts, about 479 g of filament and roughly 690 minutes (about 11.5 hours) of printing. I didn't add a bottom cover because the configurator offered no place for one on this base.",
